    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1840">

                <pb facs="1209" n="1093" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1093"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.673/62a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Morgenthau.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You are instructed to notify the Ottoman Government that this Government does not
                    acquiesce in the attempt of the Ottoman Government to abrogate the
                    Capitulations, and does not recognize that it has a right to do so or that its
                    action, being unilateral, has any effect upon the rights and privileges enjoyed
                    under those conventions. You will further state that this Government reserves
                    for the present the consideration of the grounds for its refusal to acquiesce in
                    the action of the Ottoman Government, and the right to make further
                    representations later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
